---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Cash-Out Refinance vs Rate-and-Term";
const description =
  "Compare cash-out refinance costs to a standard rate-and-term refinance. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-01-31";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/refinance-cash-out-vs-rate-term" lastUpdated={lastUpdated}>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Cash-out vs rate-term</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Cash-out refinance vs rate-and-term</h1>
    <p>
      Cash-out refinances raise your loan balance to take equity out. Rate-and-term refinances focus on lowering rate or term without
      increasing the balance. This guide helps you compare the total cost of each.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/guides/refinance-break-even">Refinance break-even</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/refinance-closing-costs">Closing costs</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/refinance">Refinance topic hub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Key differences</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Cash-out increases balance and payment, often with different pricing.</li>
      <li>Rate-and-term targets lower cost without added cash.</li>
      <li>Cash-out adds interest on the equity you take out.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How to compare fairly</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare the rate-and-term offer to your current loan first.</li>
      <li>Model the cash-out offer with the new balance and higher payment.</li>
      <li>Estimate total interest and break-even for both.</li>
      <li>Consider what you would do with the cash-out proceeds.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare total dollars paid over your horizon.</li>
      <li>Separate cash-out usage from refinance savings.</li>
      <li>Include any cash-out pricing adjustments in costs.</li>
      <li>Re-run if the cash-out amount changes.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Cash-out amount needed and its planned use.</li>
      <li>Rate and fee differences between the two options.</li>
      <li>Expected time you will keep the new loan.</li>
      <li>Impact on loan-to-value and PMI requirements.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Comparing only monthly payments without total interest.</li>
      <li>Ignoring the interest cost on the cash-out balance.</li>
      <li>Not accounting for a different fee structure for cash-out loans.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Is cash-out always more expensive?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Usually it increases total cost because the balance is higher, but it can still make sense if the cash replaces higher-rate
      debt.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Should I compare to a second loan instead?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Sometimes a home equity line or second mortgage may be cheaper. Compare the combined cost across options.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/amortization-schedule-calculator">Amortization schedule</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/refinance-rolling-costs-into-loan">Rolling costs into the loan</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/refinance-no-closing-costs-myth">No closing cost refinance</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/refinance-checklist">Refinance checklist</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/guides/refinance-break-even">Break-even guide</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/refinance-checklist">Refinance checklist</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/refinance">Refinance topic hub</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-01-31</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

